    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18661" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fosso</span></b> , āvi, ātum, 1,
			v. freq. a.
		fodio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to dig</i>, <i>pierce</i> (ante-and
			post-class.): corpora telis, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 100</span></i> (Ann. v.
			569 ed. Vahl.).—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fossātum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>a ditch</i>, <i>fosse</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. Sept.
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Capitol. Gord. 28</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 4,
			16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fossātus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a boundary</i>,
			Auct. Rei Agr. p. 254 and 267 Goes.</div>
